text:
emma: Hey, running into a streaming stall in the Node/Edge SDK on Vercel edge runtime. ReadableStream starts emitting chunks then stops after ~10s when our auth token rotates. Client never throws, stream just hangs. Anyone seen this with token rotation + SSE?

raj: Can you paste minimal repro + package versions? v0.x of SDK? edge runtime config?

emma: Using @redwood/sdk v0.9.1, Node 18 on Vercel Edge (edge function). Token rotation: we re-fetch a new token and set Authorization header on next request. Repro steps:
```
// minimal pseudo-repro
import { Redwood } from '@redwood/sdk'
export default async (req) => {
  const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY })
  const res = await client.stream.chat({ model: 'redwood-1-small', messages: [{role:'user', content:'stream test'}] })
  const reader = res.body.getReader()
  while(true){
    const { value, done } = await reader.read()
    if(done) break
    console.log('chunk', new TextDecoder().decode(value))
  }
}
```
Logs show: `401` from inference.redwood.ai right after token rotate, then client-side stream stops with no error. The server shows reconnect attempts from our client but SDK doesn't surface retries to app.

oliver: Two things to try: 1) upgrade to v0.10.0 — we fixed SSE reconnect logic + edge ReadableStream release in that one. 2) ensure you recreate the stream client after token rotation (don't mutate headers mid-stream).

emma: Will try upgrade. Is there a known race where ReadableStream.locked stays true and prevents retries?

raj: There was a bug where on 401 the SDK attempted an automatic retry but used the same locked stream reader which left the stream hanging. v0.10.0 moves retry to before handing a reader to user. Also added clearer errors when auth fails during streaming.

emma: I upgraded locally to v0.10.0 and restarted deploy — better but still seeing occasional stalls (~1 per 100 streams). Attached trace: `fetch /v1/stream 503` then `client: stream closed` but no stack.

oliver: Can you run with DEBUG=redwood:sdk to get internal lifecycle logs? Also include the exact edge runtime setting (vercel.json) and whether you're using any ReadableStream polyfills.

emma: DEBUG logs pasted: `sdk:stream life start -> handoff-reader -> stream:error 503 -> stream:closed` — nothing about retry. Our vercel.json has "runtime": "experimental-edge". No polyfills.

support-bot: Ticket created: SUP-8421 (assigned to eng-streaming).

raj: Eng note: if server returns 5xx during streaming handshake we should either surface error or attempt a fresh connection; we had a regression in the 0.9.x retry backoff. I'll file a PR to ensure on non-auth 5xx we propagate errors rather than silently closing.

emma: For our current prod workaround I decreased token rotation frequency and added a client-level backoff to recreate the whole request on any stalled stream. Ugly but unblocks.

oliver: Thanks for the repro and logs. If you can share a tiny deploy (edge function + package.json) we can reproduce on our infra and attach an integration test. In the meanwhile, try v0.10.0 and ensure you re-create the stream client after token refresh.

emma: Will do. If we still see one-per-100 after upgrade I will open the minimal deploy. Thanks all :thumbsup:

deploy-bot: Note: no platform-wide incidents currently. If we reproduce internally we'll link to SUP-8421 and escalate.
